/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Length of Last Word
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Strings
Difficulty : Easy

Problem:
Given a string containing words and spaces, return the length
of the last word.

A word is a maximal sequence of non-space characters.

Approach:
Traverse the string from the end.

First, skip all trailing spaces because they do not belong
to the last word.

Then continue moving backward while the characters are not
spaces. Count these characters until the beginning of the
string or a space is reached.

Why does this work?

The last word is located at the end of the string after all
trailing spaces are removed.

By scanning backward, we can directly find the last word
without processing unnecessary characters before it.

Algorithm:
1. Start from the last character.
2. Skip all trailing spaces.
3. Count characters until a space or the beginning is reached.
4. Return the count.

Time Complexity : O(n)

Reason:
In the worst case, every character in the string may be visited.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
Only a constant number of variables are used.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int lengthOfLastWord(string s) {

        int end = s.size() - 1;
        int wordLength = 0;

        // Skip trailing spaces.
        while (end >= 0 && s[end] == ' ') {
            end--;
        }

        // Count characters of the last word.
        while (end >= 0 && s[end] != ' ') {
            wordLength++;
            end--;
        }

        return wordLength;
    }
};
